# Slice 346 (the book, forms-declare-or-call; plan M11 5b): a place declared by the receiver of a reference is no
# Structure, and this reference points to neither a callable nor a Structure, so `p: other` neither applies anything nor
# declares: it is refused (8). A reference to an ordinary Structure launches it (R22, item 2): place_reference_launch,
# and place_reference_unknown for the former case of this file.
int: i 1
@: p int @i
p: other
int: after i
